# Refit vs plain Claude

Both start from the repo alone, in the same sandbox with the same setup. Refit runs its whole pipeline; plain Claude (claude-sonnet-5-5) gets one prompt and plain file, shell and web tools, and finds the changes itself. A blind judge (claude-opus-5-5) reads both diffs as A and B, in an order fixed per repo.

| | Refit | Plain Claude |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Judge prefers | 3 of 10 (30%) | 5 of 10 (50%) |
| Ties | 2 | 2 |
| API changes handled correctly / handled | 26 / 30 | 22 / 23 |
| Things broken or changed without need | 13 | 7 |
| Repo's own checks pass (changed repos with checks) | 6 of 6 | 6 of 6 |
| Changed a repo with no checks of its own | 3 | 3 |
| Changed nothing | 1 | 1 |
| Cost of the fix per repo | $1.06 | $0.15 |

10 repos. Refit's cost is inventory, watch, match and harness; memory learning and the advisory review are left out. The judge cost $0.72.

